# Git flow

Full details: root `README.md`. Apply to every branch, commit, PR, and **generated commit message**.

## Branches

- Land on `main` only via PR + review
- One ticket = one branch
- Feature: `feature/zetan01-<number>-<short-kebab-slug>` (English, lowercase)
- Fix with no new behavior: `fix/<short-kebab-slug>`

```text
feature/zetan01-8-home-page
fix/cart-overlay-scroll-lock
```

## Commit message generation (critical)

When suggesting or writing a commit message:

1. Inspect the **full** change set (`git status` / staged + unstaged), not one open file
2. Summarize the **main outcome** of the whole diff in one line
3. Never write `docs: update README…` if the diff also adds apps, packages, configs, tests, etc.
4. Use the project format below — not vague “update files” / “update README”

Format:

```text
<type>(<folder>): <outcome>
```

- Types: `feat` `fix` `perf` `refactor` `chore` `ci` `docs` `test` `build` `style` `revert`
- Folder = `apps/web` | `apps/api` | `packages/shared` when **one** area dominates
- Changes across monorepo root + multiple apps → **omit** `(folder)`
- After `:` lowercase outcome (what landed), not a file list
- Ticket when known: `[ZETAN01-8]`

```text
# good — scaffold spans web + api + shared + root
feat: scaffold the web/api monorepo with shared types, tooling, and docs

# good — single area
feat(apps/web): [ZETAN01-8] add the home page shell

# bad — ignores most of the diff
docs: update README.md with project overview
```

PR title = what lands on `main`; PR body follows `.github/pull_request_template.md` and always ends with screenshots (same style, or `[ZETAN01-8] Add …`).

## Never put in commits

Do **not** add to message, body, or trailers:

- `Co-authored-by: Cursor …` / `Cursor Agent …`
- `Made with Cursor` / agent signatures / AI footers
- Any other Cursor / AI co-author line

Commit only when the user explicitly asks. Do not push unless they explicitly ask to push.
